{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Of the clean beasts and of the beasts that are not clean, two by two they came to Noah</b>. Rashi explained (Rashi on Genesis 7:9): they were all equated in this number — from the minimum they were two. And others said (Radak) that the meaning of \"two\" is pairs, to say that they came male and female together. In my opinion, so it was: from all of them two, a male and a female, came of their own accord, and Noah added to bring from the clean ones six pairs, for those that came to be saved came of their own accord, but those for the purpose of sacrifice — he exerted himself in the commandment, for so he was told. And the reason for \"and Noah did according to all that YHWH commanded him\" (Genesis 7:5) — they said in Bereshit Rabbah (Bereshit Rabbah 32:5): this refers to his preparing to gather beasts and wild animals and fowl, that is, the clean ones, which he exerted himself to acquire and brought them to his house. And the verse that said a third time \"as Elohim commanded Noah\" (Genesis 7:9) — this is to say that he did as he was commanded regarding the entry into the ark, for it is attached above with \"and Noah went in,\" to say that Noah and his sons and his wife and his sons' wives came into the ark, and from the beasts and the fowl and the creeping things, two by two that came to him into the ark, and all of them came with him — that they entered the ark because of the waters of the flood, as Elohim commanded him. And he turned back and specified the month and the day on which the flood came and how it came, and said that on that very day it was that Noah came into the ark, and with him all living flesh — not before that."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:25:57.806914784Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}